      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PURPLE MOON (2) is looking to improve on her last-start fourth behind Cee Cee In Paris at Group Two level over 1609m at Menangle seven-and-a-half weeks ago. Racing in a much easier line-up and is the one to beat from an ideal draw. MISTER DEVEREAUX (8) scored at Kilmore three runs ago when leading all of the way. Returned to something like that form last time out when third over 2240m at Melton, beaten 12 metres. Shouldn't spend a penny from this draw and the sprint lane may come in handy. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. ZOOLU (6) is on the radar after her last-start fifth over 2150m at Bendigo two months ago after racing four-back on the spell at the bell. AFRICAN GALA (1) should not have any excuses from his favourable draw.",
